  "question": {
    "text": "The number of points in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>,&nbsp;for which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>,&nbsp;is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></math></p><p> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>We know that, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is positive for all real numbers, now it depends on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>. </p><p>So,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>is increasing if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>></mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is decreasing if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo> </mo><mi>x</mi><mo><</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mo>∞</mo></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>∞</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mo>∞</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>∞</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0039_5060bae492ae.png\"/></p><p>So, it is clear that graph cuts the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis at two points, so number of solutions are two.</p>"
  }
